---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const BASE = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Felix Geelhaar — writes on operations, product, engineering, and team collaboration. Builds tools for engineers working with AI agents."
  lede="The long version."
  nav="about"
>
  <section class="prose">
    <p>
      I write about the operating models, product trade-offs, and engineering practices that
      decide whether teams ship clearly. The interesting layer for me is the connective
      tissue &mdash; how decisions move, where ownership lives, what a working agreement
      actually does. Less framework, more field notes.
    </p>
    <p>
      In parallel I build tools. Mostly for engineers pairing with AI coding agents:
      <a href="https://github.com/felixgeelhaar/roady">roady</a> (plan-of-record that survives
      context resets), <a href="https://github.com/felixgeelhaar/tokenops">tokenops</a>
      (local LLM spend + rate-limit tracker), <a href="https://github.com/felixgeelhaar/scout">scout</a>
      (browser automation in one binary), <a href="https://github.com/felixgeelhaar/mnemos">mnemos</a>
      (evidence layer with claims + contradictions), and a few Go libraries around resilience and
      MCP. Everything lives on <a href="https://github.com/felixgeelhaar">GitHub</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      I live near Munich. Currently focused on the things on <a href={`${BASE}now`}>/now</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Find me elsewhere</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/felixgeelhaar">GitHub</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/felixgeelhaar/">LinkedIn</a></li>
      <li><a href={`${BASE}contact`}>Email</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
